#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:176
#: e9520daf23da48fbb3bb06b9bea15a41
msgid "This section discusses how to build the code in Qt Creator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:178
#: 5ae5b379f1e7463cb39e4cd8227c54a9
msgid "Click on **Projects** on the left pane and make sure that you are in the **Build & Run** tab page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:181
#: a5c0858a69b0434aa7e4c92a45e974c6
msgid "Click **Manage Kits** in the topleft corner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:183
#: 81baa4f6e83d4e32b019121227150323
msgid "First click on the **Compilers** tab page and then **Add** on the right hand side of the compilers list. Choose an easily recognisable name for your compiler and make sure the Compiler and Make path are referring to the executables of the PX4 toolchain (Windows) or the downloaded gcc-arm cross-compiler (Linux). Also choose \"GCC\" as the Error parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:191
#: be6789126af74fdbadf016eeee2ce021
msgid "Then click on the **Kits** tab page. Click **Add** on the right hand side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:193
#: 7403c94e53104da79ef6072f4c3ac6ca
msgid "Choose an easily recognisable name for your build kit and make sure you fill in the proper compiler (the one you just added) and the debugger inside the PX4 toolchain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:199
#: 30e1fe024071460da50a475a5537b69f
msgid "Click **Apply**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:201
#: 5c0833d37ae34b399f32e84d8d598cef
msgid "Back on the **Projects** page, click **Add Kit** and choose the Build Kit you just added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:203
#: 9b2c4e02bb2f476295322d6b815dad6b
msgid "Now you have one \"Build Configuration\" called \"Default\". You can make as many Build Configurations as you want, but we'll take the ArduCopter build as an example for now. Next to *Edit build configuration*, click on **Add** and choose **Clone Selected** in the drop down menu. Pick a name (e.g. \"Copter\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:208
#: 3e8c24db1af641c28f895c595fcb4b1b
msgid "Click on the **Details** of the *Build Steps* and type \"px4-v2 -j2\" as *Make arguments*. Deselect the **Targets**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:211
#: 276b0ac5530945c8a8ddf89e24cec0d6
msgid "Click on the **Details** of the *Clean Steps* and type \"px4-clean\" as *Make arguments*. Deselect the **Targets**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:217
#: 5c6393298fb14487b8574231919744e4
msgid "You can make other build configurations for e.g. ArduPlane in the same way. You can quickly switch between \"Build Configurations\" by clicking the logo just above the **Run** icon (the green arrow) on the left pane."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:221
#: c847dec6d5ba45e0b78865b4df4db4ee
msgid "You can now remove the MSVC or standard GCC build kit (click on the down arrow on the kit itself and choose **Remove Kit**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:224
#: 9281a3e609f04f86ab0b33f8cae53b2e
msgid "You're now ready to build the code. Click on **Edit** in the left pane to edit the code and browse through the project. Click **Build project-name** in the *Build* menu (or Ctrl+B) to build the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:228
#: 0504dcb2f1af479b9610ad3785736507
msgid "Apply coding style guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:229
#: 83fedc12542c475188c5a372856829e1
msgid "It is useful that the Qt Creator editor is configured so that it automatically applies the layout guidelines described in :ref:`ArduPilot Style Guide <style-guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:232
#: cde1400946b744fd931c8e114dc41c41
msgid "Indentation: Click on the **Tools** menu and choose **Options**. Subsequently, pick the **Text Editor** view and then the **Behaviour** tab page. You can set the tab policy (spaces only) and the size of a tab and indentations (4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:236
#: 8786dfd3e7d64ccd94501f728ea93d9d
msgid "Other interesting settings can be found in the **C++** view in the same *Options* dialog. You can define how specific parts of your code will be aligned (e.g. assignments, switch/cases, control statements, braces, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/building-px4-with-qtcreator.rst:239
#: 7393301af3934aeeae929e1310c62409
msgid "Commenting: In order to comply with the coding guidelines , you will need to provide documentation in Doxygen format. Qt Creator will automatically generate a Doxygen documentation template if you type ``/**`` before the definition of the class, function, ..."
msgstr ""
